  "geometryBasis": "Original named monastery way361128301/Q541696 establishes complex identity/site boundary; ten individual building/roof ways define actual church, enclosing cell/house/gate/museum wings and covered walk. Original named west-gate entrance node fixes the approach.",
  "authoringDirection": "Build the signed individual church and monastic-wing plans around the real open court. Church is double-aisle, about20m east-west by14m north-south, with WEST front: two recessed doors/oculi and blind central niche, engaged columns/cornices, twin curved gables/pinnacles and an open2+1bell gable/central circular void. Pale limestone church, warm rubble enclosing wings with simple dressed openings/parapets. Respect explicit roof/wall=no covered walks as open structures. Use reasonable medium-fi height estimates(~7mchurch body,~13.5mbell crown, mostlytwo-storey~7mouter wings) and record unmeasured details. Never extrude the monastery site parcel or seal the court; detached ossuary/restaurant/service buildings and1866battle reconstruction excluded.",
